{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things","id":1193762,"title":"Help me understand a few things","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-09T17:50:20-08:00","id":1193762,"title":"Help me understand a few things","content":"So i am having a few lingering hangups about Beast. Elements i'm still struggling to understand.<br /> <br /> First fair warning (?) i started with a very negative view about Beast and i have mostly come around. I'm afraid i am still not 100% behind the game. Some things that, if i run a game, i would either avoid/ignore or maybe outright change. But i am making effort to ... get the game because i do believe there is something there that i want to play.<br /> All that said, lets get to it.<br /> <br /> The 3 points i dont quite understand.<br /> <br /> 1- Relation between hunger and choice.<br /> Okay lets see if i can explain that well.<br /> From what i understand there is 2 parts to feeding. What i call the core (the hunger), like a hunger for ruin and what i call the scheme, that is the particular way you feed.<br /> So from what i understand the core (the hunger) is innate to the horror the Beast gets. But what exactly determines the scheme?<br /> Say you have two Beast with a hunger for ruins what determines that one needs to destroy kneecaps and the other needs to destroy expectations? Is it a choice? Can it be changed?<br /> <br /> 2- I don't get what a makara is.<br /> Its stupid i know but ... is it really just about being an aquatic monster? For monsters representing types of fear, you can have an aquatic monster from every other families.<br /> Anakim: 2 things here fits. Either the giant whate/leviathan. So huge that you are helpless against it. Or i feel that the fear of the vastness of the ocean is very fitting as an anakim concept.<br /> Eshmaki: Water obscure vision very very well. Especially at night. Say your somehow reading this while in the ocean at night, there could be a shark literally next to your leg and you wouldnt know it. That feels very eshmaki.<br /> Namtaru: Just google Blobfish. Try not do it while eating.<br /> Ugallu: There is no cover on the ocean. You are quite literally exposed to everything that swims there. And swimming is relatively kind of like flying... i guess. (okay ugallu might be my weakest one here).<br /> So what is left for the makara to represent?<br /> <br /> 3- The family aspect in Beast.<br /> That one makes me feel a bit stupid as the book keeps talking about Beast being a family and i just dont see it. Like at all. I'll admit i dont even know where to begin with that one. I get with werewolf the concept of the pack as a foster family. I even get how the concept work with vampire. But with Beast. It flies right over me.<br /> <br /> Even if i dont solve all of these, i'll still be very satisfied seeing your thoughts on the subjects.<br /> <br /> As always, thx for the help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T17:57:29-08:00","id":1193763,"title":"","content":"I always imagine beast as weird yandere stalkers that everyone just lets them hang out because there kinda of afraid of them the .makara repsent the fear of figuratively like drowning under stress depression and all that other bullshit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T18:56:53-08:00","id":1193774,"title":"","content":"As to your first question: The specific nuance of a Hunger is left up to the player to decide. In universe it's usually presented as some mixture of Horrors being picky eaters when they can afford to be and Beasts not always being comfortable with the more exacting demands. So a Horror may favor one very specific type of destruction, but that's an ethical line the Beast would rather not cross and so they end up picking an alternative method that both can live with.<br /> <br /> For the second: One of the nice things about Beast is that it's conceptually broad enough to represent most any monster a number of different ways. Makara can represent a hostile environment humans aren't adapted to, crushing pressure either literal or figurative, being overwhelmed with tasks you aren't equipped to handle.<br /> <br /> And for the third: Being a Beast can be a hard, scary, lonely experience. Finding somebody else like you, somebody who understands what you're going through is a Big Deal. I think that theme runs pretty true throughout CoD in general. Monsters gravitate toward other similar monsters because being an outsider is difficult and lonely and while they may not be fully human most of them are still subject to that aspect of the human condition. Seriously, you have this problem that sets you apart from your old friends and family, puts them at risk, makes it so you can never safely let any of them get truly close to you. Might end in a lunatic murdering you just for existing. Learning you don't have to face that alone is huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T19:11:14-08:00","id":1193776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things#post1193762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i am having a few lingering hangups about Beast. Elements i'm still struggling to understand.<br /> <br /> First fair warning (?) i started with a very negative view about Beast and i have mostly come around. I'm afraid i am still not 100% behind the game. Some things that, if i run a game, i would either avoid/ignore or maybe outright change. But i am making effort to ... get the game because i do believe there is something there that i want to play.<br /> All that said, lets get to it.<br /> <br /> The 3 points i dont quite understand.<br /> <br /> 1- Relation between hunger and choice.<br /> Okay lets see if i can explain that well.<br /> From what i understand there is 2 parts to feeding. What i call the core (the hunger), like a hunger for ruin and what i call the scheme, that is the particular way you feed.<br /> So from what i understand the core (the hunger) is innate to the horror the Beast gets. But what exactly determines the scheme?<br /> Say you have two Beast with a hunger for ruins what determines that one needs to destroy kneecaps and the other needs to destroy expectations? Is it a choice? Can it be changed?<br /> <br /> 2- I don't get what a makara is.<br /> Its stupid i know but ... is it really just about being an aquatic monster? For monsters representing types of fear, you can have an aquatic monster from every other families.<br /> Anakim: 2 things here fits. Either the giant whate/leviathan. So huge that you are helpless against it. Or i feel that the fear of the vastness of the ocean is very fitting as an anakim concept.<br /> Eshmaki: Water obscure vision very very well. Especially at night. Say your somehow reading this while in the ocean at night, there could be a shark literally next to your leg and you wouldnt know it. That feels very eshmaki.<br /> Namtaru: Just google Blobfish. Try not do it while eating.<br /> Ugallu: There is no cover on the ocean. You are quite literally exposed to everything that swims there. And swimming is relatively kind of like flying... i guess. (okay ugallu might be my weakest one here).<br /> So what is left for the makara to represent?<br /> <br /> 3- The family aspect in Beast.<br /> That one makes me feel a bit stupid as the book keeps talking about Beast being a family and i just dont see it. Like at all. I'll admit i dont even know where to begin with that one. I get with werewolf the concept of the pack as a foster family. I even get how the concept work with vampire. But with Beast. It flies right over me.<br /> <br /> Even if i dont solve all of these, i'll still be very satisfied seeing your thoughts on the subjects.<br /> <br /> As always, thx for the help.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOkay, I'll give this a try and hope I help clear up some problems:<br /> <br /> 1)<br /> \u200bA Beasts Hunger is inherent to the Beast (for more specifically, the Horror that is the Beast's soul). How a Beast feeds a particular Hunger is however the Beast's choice. Using Ruin as an example, a Beast is compelled to feed by destroying something, what they destroy is up to the Beast, not the Horror. Meaning that a Beast could just feed by breaking the kneecaps of a athletic hopeful (thus destroying his hopes and dreams), by posting spoilers all over the net (thus destroying expectations), or by throwing bricks through rich people's windows (thus destroying their sense of security). What a Beast Hungers for is set in stone, how they feed that hunger is entirely their choice.<br /> <br /> 2)<br /> \u200bWith Makara, their fear is drowning, whether drowning in literally in water or drowning in debt, despair, or pressure. For Makara, the deep can be symbolic or literal. The other families don't represent the fear of unfathomable depths, crushing pressure, and the siren call of the abyss quite as well as Makara.<br /> <br /> 3)<br /> \u200bThe Family aspect comes from the idea that Beasts are all related, at least spiritually, to each other and to the other monsters of the Chronicles of Darkness (Demons and Instatiables excluded). The fact that they can all relate the feeling of having a ravenous monster living in their soul that compels them to hurt people and constantly being attacked by psychos declaring, &quot;Die monster, you don't belong in this world!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bFor Beasts, they have incentives to gather together, much as Werewolves, Vampires, Mages, Changelings, Demons, and Hunters. For defense, to pool resources, and emotional support.<br /> <br /> \u200bI hope some of what I said might have been helpful Maitrecorbo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":". 03-09-2018, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T19:26:42-08:00","id":1193778,"title":"","content":"Let me see if I can help a bit. <br /> 1) The player's guide actually addresses this and the answer ends up with, &quot;We don't know.&quot; It's one of the major mysteries for Beast's that look at it as they all understand the Hunger is just an inherent part of being one of the Beghotten, but they don't actually know why one Beast revels in chasing down the prey and ripping their heart out of their chest and another collects wedding rings. Let along the odd divides that come from why one nemesis will only punish etiquette blunders and another a chamber in Quebec because punishing smugglers keeps making them the central point on cartel wars. <br /> <br /> So not really a choice, at least not as far as anyone in canon is aware. If you walk the path of hunger on the way to incarnation you'll probably come to your own conclusions and understanding about it for your game. Change is noted as a thing that does happen, it just isn't common. Sometimes it's a minor change you know a ravager changes what they need to ruin and other times its more extreme and a tyrant becomes an enabler. Again by no means common, but not unheard of for it to happen.<br /> <br /> 2) Water and the ocean is the most literal aspect of it. It tends to come out more as being overwhelmed, things you can struggle against and still lose to because it just keeps coming and eventually it'll either overtake you or you'll make a mistake and then there will be no coming back. The main difference between the Anakim and the Makara in this respect would be how futile the struggle is. An Anakim is a tidal wave there is no fighting a tidal there is only escape or being destroyed by it. The Makara are holes in the boat fighting isn't impossible, it may not even be a bad idea if you act quickly enough you can plug it. If there are too many, if the patch doesn't hold, if you don't act quickly enough then it can be just as dooming as that tidal wave.<br /> <br /> It is also the fear of the depths, thing that are buried and gone away. Think of it like this a Makara whisperer drags out those old secrets secrets and nightmares that you were sure were long gone. <br /> <br /> 3) Beasts are predominatly looking for places to belong, for others to watch their backs and help with their goals. I kind of think what Beasts tend to be looking for is closer to the nakama concept as you see it in a bunch of anime. So less all monsters are my family, or even the garou are my family and more, &quot;So I know this glass walker, goes by the handle Mokie online, she's solid. Rest of her pack are kind of douchebags to me, but Mokie and I are tight and in a pinch I think we're both sure the other will come through.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T19:34:14-08:00","id":1193780,"title":"","content":"So for the Makara thing, i think you guys homed in on something i didnt realize. <br /> I've had alot of nightmares in my life, but everytime water was involved it was related to a fear best represented by one of the other families. The fear of the vastness of the ocean and my insignificance compared to it or the fear of not being able to see whats in the water around me have been nightmares i've had frequently. But for as long as i can remember, i've never drowned when water was involved in my nightmares. Which, writing this i notice how freaking weird this is. That means, at a deep psychological level i just don't associate water (sea, ocean, rivers) with drowning. uh...<br /> <br /> So what if i have the concept of an eshmaki that is aquatic? Am i just hosed? Cause all the aquatic atavism are in the makara line. <br /> Say a crocodilian monster with the lair being a murky river that the horror hides in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T19:50:56-08:00","id":1193782,"title":"","content":"Not totally hosed, but they will cost more as out-of-family atavisms. You can also remodel some of the eshmaki stuff to have more of a water theme.<br /> <br /> Also, remember Lair Traits. None of them have any connection to one Family specifically, and they provide useful environmental immunities too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T19:52:06-08:00","id":1193784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193780#post1193780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for the Makara thing, i think you guys homed in on something i didnt realize.<br /> I've had alot of nightmares in my life, but everytime water was involved it was related to a fear best represented by one of the other families. The fear of the vastness of the ocean and my insignificance compared to it or the fear of not being able to see whats in the water around me have been nightmares i've had frequently. But for as long as i can remember, i've never drowned when water was involved in my nightmares. Which, writing this i notice how freaking weird this is. That means, at a deep psychological level i just don't associate water (sea, ocean, rivers) with drowning. uh...</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusing. If I recall correctly the tribe in Shakeshpear in the Bush actually had a problem with one part of MacBeth because their tribe believed that a person could not drown unless it was caused by a witch. So yeah funny how that happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193780#post1193780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what if i have the concept of an eshmaki that is aquatic? Am i just hosed? Cause all the aquatic atavism are in the makara line.<br /> Say a crocodilian monster with the lair being a murky river that the horror hides in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then go for it man. An atavism being in a line doesn't mean that's the only line that can have that power, think of it more as being iconic of those lines. Cause if we go with real animals I associate the horeshoe crab with the Eshmaki over the Makara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T19:57:02-08:00","id":1193786,"title":"","content":"1 - I believe the choice is a result of personal preference, rather than having anything to do with being a Beast. The core book makes a point that the Horror doesn't actually care how you feed, only that you continue to do so. That being said, there is a difference between a sirloin steak and a cheese burger. Sure, they're both made of beef and will fill you up if you eat them. But one is a high class meal, while the other is a greasy sandwich.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - The Makara are descended from sea monsters, but that's not all that they are. Some have migrated to dry land, just like some fish crawled out of the sea and evolved legs. The way I interpret Makara is that they are the fear of being in a hostile environment, one in which you are ill equipped to survive in. If you were to pluck a human from New York City and drop them in the heart of the Amazon Rainforest with nothing but what they immediately had on them at the time, then chances are they would be dead before the end of the week. Same thing as dropping them in the middle of the ocean, or an abandoned mine shaft. And it doesn't have to be physical depths, either. Your Makara could immerse people in social-political situations that they were unprepared for, plunging them into a metaphorical kind of depths.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3 - As for the family aspect, the best I can tell you is that there are an awful lot of cultures who believe in a mythical progenitor of all monsters. Whatever name you wish to go by, they share a core theme of being the mother / father of ALL monsters. It seems like Beast decides to incorporate this mythology into its setting, so that vampires, werewolves, faeries, est are all literally family. If they go back far enough, they can trace their origins back to a single progenitor, and it is that progenitor that the Beasts know to be the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> Whether or not the other splats acknowledge the validity of this story is up to the individual, rather than society as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T20:00:21-08:00","id":1193788,"title":"","content":"Ugh shameful confession here. I completely forgot you could buy atavism out of family.<br /> '' At least one of your starting atavism must be aligned wit your family'' p. 79<br /> That solves like ... 90 % of difficulties i had with character creation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the makara, while i still feel that things like the abyss and the depth feels more eshmaki. The whole suffocation aspect is something i can work with.<br /> As an aside, instead of water could one have the depth of space as a possible makara environment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 03-09-2018, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T20:22:58-08:00","id":1193792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193788#post1193788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh shameful confession here. I completely forgot you could buy atavism out of family.<br /> '' At least one of your starting atavism must be aligned wit your family'' p. 79<br /> That solves like ... 90 % of difficulties i had with character creation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the makara, while i still feel that things like the abyss and the depth feels more eshmaki. The whole suffocation aspect is something i can work with.<br /> As an aside, instead of water could one have the depth of space as a possible makara environment?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said, I interpret Makara as being the fear of a foreign environment. One which you are poorly suited to live in.<br /> <br /> From my personal experience, I've found that you can greatly expand the possibilities of just about all the families if you look at them from a <b>metaphorical perspective.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Anakim aren't the fear of giants coming in to eat our cattle and smash our cities. They're the fear of being powerless to defend ourselves.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki aren't the fear of darkness. They're the fear of what lurks inside the darkness, just waiting until we aren't looking before they strike.<br /> <br /> Ugallu aren't the fear of flying monsters. They're the fear of exposure, and being unable to sense the threat until it's too late.<br /> <br /> Namtaru are... well, they're pretty much exactly what they represent, the fear of that which we find revolting. But the trick is that revulsion doesn't necessarily have to be turned outward in order to get the point across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T20:29:30-08:00","id":1193796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193788#post1193788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh shameful confession here. I completely forgot you could buy atavism out of family.<br /> '' At least one of your starting atavism must be aligned wit your family'' p. 79<br /> That solves like ... 90 % of difficulties i had with character creation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We've all been somewhere similar before. Way too often do you forget that things costing more out of favor doesn't mean you can't buy them even if you normally don't. Happens all the time in older dnd where if a character can't favor a skill they don't have ranks in that skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193788#post1193788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the makara, while i still feel that things like the abyss and the depth feels more eshmaki. The whole suffocation aspect is something i can work with.<br /> As an aside, instead of water could one have the depth of space as a possible makara environment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I think at least one or two space themed horrors were made in the character concept thread based off Makara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T20:54:24-08:00","id":1193802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193780#post1193780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for the Makara thing, i think you guys homed in on something i didnt realize.<br /> I've had alot of nightmares in my life, but everytime water was involved it was related to a fear best represented by one of the other families. The fear of the vastness of the ocean and my insignificance compared to it or the fear of not being able to see whats in the water around me have been nightmares i've had frequently. But for as long as i can remember, i've never drowned when water was involved in my nightmares. Which, writing this i notice how freaking weird this is. That means, at a deep psychological level i just don't associate water (sea, ocean, rivers) with drowning. uh...<br /> <br /> So what if i have the concept of an eshmaki that is aquatic? Am i just hosed? Cause all the aquatic atavism are in the makara line.<br /> Say a crocodilian monster with the lair being a murky river that the horror hides in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You get to start with two Atavisms and only one needs to be of your family. You could take an Eshmaki Atavism and then maybe pick up Heart of the Ocean.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah, you noticed that. I needed to refresh the page before I commented...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 03-09-2018, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T22:28:42-08:00","id":1193818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193780#post1193780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for the Makara thing, i think you guys homed in on something i didnt realize.<br /> I've had alot of nightmares in my life, but everytime water was involved it was related to a fear best represented by one of the other families. The fear of the vastness of the ocean and my insignificance compared to it or the fear of not being able to see whats in the water around me have been nightmares i've had frequently. But for as long as i can remember, i've never drowned when water was involved in my nightmares. Which, writing this i notice how freaking weird this is. That means, at a deep psychological level i just don't associate water (sea, ocean, rivers) with drowning. uh...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's actually not that weird. Whenever I dream of being in water, I always have the power to breathe while submerged. In my dreams, water is literally as breathable as air, so I've never had a dream of drowning before, either.<br /> <br /> It's the fear of everything else inside the water that concerns me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T23:32:53-08:00","id":1193827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193796#post1193796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh yeah I think at least one or two space themed horrors were made in the character concept thread based off Makara.</div> </div> </div> </div>We even made a couple of Atavisms for them in the Other Atavism Ideas thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T12:05:23-08:00","id":1194000,"title":"","content":"So, recapping a little<br /> <br /> 1- The answers so far are : Yes, No, Maybe, I mean a little.<br /> I'm not being snarky. I've studied in philosophy so i am used that sometimes these are the answers you get. <br /> The good thing is that (in the event i run a game) i'll go with what i'm most comfortable with.<br /> <br /> 2- So i can take away the ocean part of the makara and apply it to other families with no problem. What stays with the makara is the concept of depth. The depth of the ocean yes, but would also work with the heart of the jungle (maybe?), the depth of space and the abyss within the mountain???<br /> <br /> 3- To me alot of what is being proposed here is more to do with friendship and community. Family doesnt always understand you or share the same interest or pains. Or rather for me these things do not represent what family is. I see it a bit in regards with the rest of the supernaturals tho. <br /> Apologies, i know you tried but i just dont get it as a bond for a group of Beast. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T12:37:29-08:00","id":1194009,"title":"","content":"A Beast's Lair is practically a part of their soul. When a Brood connects their lairs, they basically connect their souls.<br /> Beasts are family, they share similarities, recognize each other, and can relate to each other better than anyone else in most regards. On the other hand, family squabbles and fights, and family fights can be the nastiest. True for beasts, too. They can even invade each others souls, and hurt each other in ways most others cannot precise because of that inherent understanding. Just like family.<br /> That doesn't mean others cant understand the beast better than Begotten in some cases- Predators and uratha will find a lot of common ground, and vampire and tyrants probably share more common ground than they do with collectors.<br /> Just like you may have some more things in common with friends than with family.<br /> in essence, Beasts share common roots, and they feel that pull as anyone else does when they meet their family.<br /> Did that help any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T13:02:27-08:00","id":1194014,"title":"","content":"I see, but couldnt you replace Beasts with Prometheans or any of the other splat and say the exact same thing? Then why is the theme of family specially pushed for Beasts.<br /> <br /> Honestly i'm beginning to think that i am overthinking this. Everything the books (and the people here describe) evokes to me more the concept of community than family. But maybe thats the thing, it evokes for me the same thing as with anybody else but i just happen to associate a different word to it (community instead of family). <br /> Am i making any sense here? I feel like i am rambling a bit.<br /> <br /> Btw yes it is helping. thank you. I just hope people understand that i am not voluntarily being obtuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T15:45:16-08:00","id":1194067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194014#post1194014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, but couldnt you replace Beasts with Prometheans or any of the other splat and say the exact same thing? Then why is the theme of family specially pushed for Beasts.<br /> <br /> Honestly i'm beginning to think that i am overthinking this. Everything the books (and the people here describe) evokes to me more the concept of community than family. But maybe thats the thing, it evokes for me the same thing as with anybody else but i just happen to associate a different word to it (community instead of family).<br /> Am i making any sense here? I feel like i am rambling a bit.<br /> <br /> Btw yes it is helping. thank you. I just hope people understand that i am not voluntarily being obtuse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not really, due to the nature in which Prometheans work. The other splats are all about finding a way to cope with existence as a monster, Prometheans are about finding a way to cure it. They want to become humans, and their story revolves around the quest for a soul of their own. They also have a supernatural force that compels people to hate them, despite their best efforts. The other splats are feared and hated, sure, but that's more due to their behavioral consequences, rather than some eldritch power making people react to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> One aspect of family is that Beasts have the unique ability to evolve their powers through their bonds with each other. The more time they spend around other supernatural creatures, the more Nightmares they can discover and add to their list of powers. The core book encourages players to create their own Nightmares and Atavisms, offering a wider variety than what is presented in canon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T17:05:44-08:00","id":1194090,"title":"","content":"Also be mindful that the Horror's and the Lair's shape and features are based on dream logic, hence eminently malleable. When the Beast learns new tricks in terms of Atavisms, including out-of-family ones, the Horror and/or the Lair may transform to reflect that. When the Ugallu learns Heart of the Ocean, their roc Horror learns to dive in the depths and takes a little bit of the leviathan aspect, or perhaps their Lair manifested a watery feature. If the Makara learns Wings of the Raptor, the opposite happens to the Horror, or perhaps their Lair developed some windy aspect. Moreover, several Horror archetypes are conceptually and mystically vast and flexible enough to encompass most or almost all Atavisms in their thematic purview and potentially belong in many Families in the first place. Dragons are the most iconic example of such a catch-all Horror, but others exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 03-10-2018, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T21:51:12-08:00","id":1194136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193780#post1193780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what if i have the concept of an eshmaki that is aquatic? Am i just hosed? Cause all the aquatic atavism are in the makara line.<br /> Say a crocodilian monster with the lair being a murky river that the horror hides in.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the big thing to remember is that Eshmaki are <i>not</i> nightmares of being hunted, or nightmares of predators. The Lurkers are nightmares of <i>darkness</i>, so when coming up with your concept, it needs to be sure to take that into account. They're the fear of <i>things </i>being out there, hidden, things that can kill you without a thought. Eshmaki stalk and strike while remaining out of their quarry's sight. That's the important part: attacking before the enemy can see you. Whether that's done through stealth, moving so fast the enemy can't react or being so innocuous that the prey doesn't realize what you are until it's too late...<br /> <br /> In this case, I think a monstrous crocodile is a <i>fantastic </i>idea for a Horror, and it totally can work with Eshmaki! You definitely want to emphasize the aspects that play up that fear of being attacked out of nowhere. A crocodile is good for that, because they're known for floating or sitting motionless, appearing to be harmless logs, or being juuuuust under the surface of the water. When their prey gets too close, they snap their jaws far faster than you would expect and then go back to being &quot;just part of the scenery.&quot;<br /> <br /> You describe your Lair as a murky river, which works well! That would probably be the Flooded Trait, representing the Chamber having a river running through it that intruders must contend with. Have you thought of other traits? (You get two to start with!) Downpour might be a fun one; it represents constant heavy rain, not strong enough to do damage, but that can make it hard to hear and see things. That would work well with your crocodile Horror; while crocs aren't exactly stealthy normally, it would help create those moments where the Heroes stop to rest next to a big fallen tree...only to realize the tree is <i>you</i>. The important part is that they don't see you until the violence begins.<br /> <br /> As for Atavisms, representing your Horror's physical abilities, I think there's several options you can go with. One of the two starting ones must be from the Eshmaki's family trait list; the other one can be anything. I'd suggest Heart of the Ocean for the first one; while it's from the Makara list, it gives you a strong set of abilities related to swimming and hunting in the water. For the second, you could either go with Limb from Limb, representing your toothy maw, or a new option from the Beast Player's Guide called Ravenous Maw, which allows you to open your jaws wiiide and swallow anything, no matter how dangerous (or alive...) Both of those would fulfill your Family Atavism. Future additions could be Unbreakable (to represent a scaly, impenetrable hide) and Monster from the Deep (in your case, a mighty sweep of your tail)!<br /> <br /> Of course, all of this is just suggestions. One of the beautiful things about <i>Beast </i>is that it's versatile and that there are so many options! Hope this helps, or at least sparks your own ideas about stuff you can do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T01:33:23-08:00","id":1194185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194136#post1194136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Lurkers are nightmares of <i>darkness</i>, so when coming up with your concept, it needs to be sure to take that into account. They're the fear of <i>things </i>being out there, hidden, things that can kill you without a thought. Eshmaki stalk and strike while remaining out of their quarry's sight. That's the important part: attacking before the enemy can see you. Whether that's done through stealth, moving so fast the enemy can't react or being so innocuous that the prey doesn't realize what you are until it's too late...</div> </div> </div> </div>In the final edition, Lurker are nightmares of Destrucion, not Darknes. Good points for your sugestion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:02:14-07:00","id":1194316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194185#post1194185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the final edition, Lurker are nightmares of Destrucion, not Darknes. Good points for your sugestion!</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that? I used my printed copy of the corebook to write all that, and it definitely says &quot;Nightmares of Darkness.&quot; Are you thinking of Ravagers, the Hunger for Ruin? OP didn't mention having a Hunger in mind for their Beast, so I didn't address it. (Though, the Horror I described probably Hungers for Prey... You could <i>maybe </i>swing it as a Tyrant, if you focused on the idea of it being the &quot;absolute ruler&quot; of its river/swamp)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:14:49-07:00","id":1194320,"title":"","content":"So, i think i've just clicked for the whole family shtick.<br /> I was seeing it to much from the human perspective. I didnt much account that the Horrors would consider themselves siblings/family and that would trickle down to the human consciousness of the .... host. (is the human side called anything? i mean theres the horror and the beast is the mix of the two but is the human half called anything?).<br /> Ugh, i dont feel like i'm explaining that very well. But i get the family aspect now at least. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194316#post1194316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Though, the Horror I described probably Hungers for Prey... You could <i>maybe </i>swing it as a Tyrant, if you focused on the idea of it being the &quot;absolute ruler&quot; of its river/swamp)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i was more imagining a hunger for prey. Tho i dont know what particular scheme he'd use. Or is lurking in the water for the unsuspecting to lunge at and drag in water be enough for a feeding scheme?<br /> Alternatively i could see a hunger for ruin working by him disliking when humans use boats on his river and wrecking them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:15:11-07:00","id":1194321,"title":"","content":"&lt;reread &gt; You are right...! On page 125, &quot; From the Shadow&quot;, say Destruction but the page 28 say Darkness. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:46:13-07:00","id":1194330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194320#post1194320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (is the human side called anything? i mean theres the horror and the beast is the mix of the two but is the human half called anything?).<br /> Ugh, i dont feel like i'm explaining that very well. But i get the family aspect now at least. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Human side = Beast/Begotten/Children<br /> <br /> Supernatural side = Horror","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:56:42-07:00","id":1194335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194320#post1194320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah i was more imagining a hunger for prey. Tho i dont know what particular scheme he'd use. Or is lurking in the water for the unsuspecting to lunge at and drag in water be enough for a feeding scheme?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actual crocs are mostly ambush predators, but Predator Beasts tend to like stalking their prey a little more actively than that.<br /> <br /> Here's a suggestion: take Maze as your second Lair Trait to start. Your character lures/chases victims into a place where he can one a Primordial Pathway to his Lair; his Brood could help him with this. Once in the Lair, the victim becomes lost inside in the Lair while your Beast (now merged with his Horror) quietly follows them,: if the victim looks back, all they see is a floating log, or maybe a few ripples in the water. Only when the victim's having a total breakdown due to not being able to find a way out of this swamp does the Beast strike.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:41:54-07:00","id":1194346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193780#post1193780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what if i have the concept of an eshmaki that is aquatic? Am i just hosed? Cause all the aquatic atavism are in the makara line.<br /> Say a crocodilian monster with the lair being a murky river that the horror hides in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I mean two of the makara atavisms don't have anything to do with water per se and would be unsuited for a crocodile (Alien Allure, and Siren's Song). On the other hand at least two eshamik atavisms would be perfectly suited for a crocodile: limb from limb, because the scariest thing of a crocodile is its maw, and relentless hunter - those things may not look like it but they can get really fast, and completely in line with the atavisms crocodiles can go very long time without food.<br /> <br /> So at character creation you could choose limb from limb as your mandatory in-family atavism, and choose heart of the ocean to get the amphibian nature of the crocodile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:44:20-07:00","id":1194347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatthiasThalmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194346#post1194346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. I mean two of the makara atavisms don't have anything to do with water per se and would be unsuited for a crocodile (Alien Allure, and Siren's Song). On the other hand at least two eshamik atavisms would be perfectly suited for a crocodile: limb from limb, because the scariest thing of a crocodile is its maw, and relentless hunter - those things may not look like it but they can get really fast, and completely in line with the atavisms crocodiles can go very long time without food.<br /> <br /> So at character creation you could choose limb from limb as your mandatory in-family atavism, and choose heart of the ocean to get the amphibian nature of the crocodile.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could probably give a crocodile Unbreakable as well, for the scales. Those are <i>tough</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T13:53:18-07:00","id":1194350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194320#post1194320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah i was more imagining a hunger for prey. Tho i dont know what particular scheme he'd use. Or is lurking in the water for the unsuspecting to lunge at and drag in water be enough for a feeding scheme?<br /> Alternatively i could see a hunger for ruin working by him disliking when humans use boats on his river and wrecking them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one thing to keep in mind is that most feeding will probably done in &quot;human&quot; form; that is, you don't need to feed in your Lair, as your Horror unless that's specifically what you want. This goes back to the &quot;<i>Beast</i> is figurative&quot; point I made earlier; you're feeding your monster soul by essentially re-enacting the sort of thing <i>it</i> would do, but in the &quot;real world.&quot;<br /> <br /> Example: An Eshmaki Predator (a Nightmare of Darkness with the Hunger for Prey) feeds by hunting down hunters. For this session, she follows a deer hunter out of town to the woods where he's planning to set up camp. That night, when he's set up in a tree to wait for the deer to wander by, she stalks around him, making just enough noise to let him know <i>something</i> is out there with him, but without letting him see her. (she can do this through both mundane stealth and her supernatural powers)<br /> <br /> Eventually, he gets freaked out enough to come down and try and make it back to vehicle \u2014 only to find that she hot-wired the truck and moved it without him noticing. He starts panicking, firing into the darkness, and she hits him with a Nightmare right before knocking him unconscious. As he fades into blackness, she whispers, &quot;There's always a better hunter...&quot; (this is her Lesson)<br /> <br /> Of course, the method Mad_Maudlin suggested also works really well! There are merits to both approaches. Staying human is simpler, and keeps people away from your Lair, where you're most vulnerable. (remember, the more you open Primordial Pathways to a Chamber, the easier it is for others to do the same thing) Taking things into the Primordial Dream lets you take on your Horror form, granting you a lot more power, and gives you total control over the environment. (you can let Tilts do a lot of the work) You also avoid the whole &quot;forensic evidence&quot; thing, especially if your Hunger is the kind that leaves bodies, rather than scared, but potentially wiser, prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T14:10:46-07:00","id":1194359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatthiasThalmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194346#post1194346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. I mean two of the makara atavisms don't have anything to do with water per se and would be unsuited for a crocodile (Alien Allure, and Siren's Song).</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind when i said that i hadnt realized that a) you could buy atavism at an out-of-family cost and b) you can start with any atavism you want as long as one of them is from your family.<br /> That was dumb of me :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T09:24:33-07:00","id":1194867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1193792#post1193792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, I interpret Makara as being the fear of a foreign environment. One which you are poorly suited to live in.<br /> <br /> From my personal experience, I've found that you can greatly expand the possibilities of just about all the families if you look at them from a <b>metaphorical perspective.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>As I've put it myself, the Anakim are scary because they're huge and unstoppable, the Namtaru are scary because they're gross and wrong, the Eshmaki are scary because they're behind you right now, and the Ugallu are scary because they can see you wherever you try to hide - in that vein, the Makara are scary because they represent a world that's inimical to you. (And Inguma are scary because they could be anyone).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193762-help-me-understand-a-few-things?p=1194000#post1194000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2- So i can take away the ocean part of the makara and apply it to other families with no problem. What stays with the makara is the concept of depth. The depth of the ocean yes, but would also work with the heart of the jungle (maybe?), the depth of space and the abyss within the mountain???</div> </div> </div> </div>Another side to it is that you have to take a step into the Makara's depths for them to affect you. You're safe from the sea monster if you don't go near the sea (though of course, when a Makara is present, you're <i>always</i> near the sea). More metaphorically, debt can't drown you if you don't get into it. Relationships can't smother you if you hold yourself alone. The problem is that the sea holds riches and resources, debt is sometimes the only way to get something you need, and relationships are a source of comfort, belonging, and help. Makara are the fear that taking risks just leads to destruction rather than reward.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}